WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.538
A shortcode is a name in square brackets that an editor types into content.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:09.796
Shortcode Templates lets you write your own in the admin, with Liquid.

00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:13.493
In this video, you create one, use it in an article, and see

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:15.230
what a template can read.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.508
An editor writes a shortcode in the body of a content item:

00:00:23.508 --> 00:00:28.544
a name, optional arguments, and optional text between an opening and a closing tag.

00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:33.750
When the item is displayed, Orchard Core replaces it with the output of the shortcode.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.581
A shortcode can be code that a module registers.

00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:40.890
With Shortcode Templates, it can also be a template:

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.541
Liquid that you write in the admin and save with the site.

00:00:44.541 --> 00:00:46.880
Editors find both in the same list.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.930
A template receives three values.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:54.764
Args holds the named arguments, Content holds the text between the tags, and

00:00:54.764 --> 00:01:00.130
Context holds what the caller passes along, such as the content item being displayed.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.904
Shortcode Templates belongs to the Shortcodes module.

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:10.857
Under Tools, Features, search for shortcode.

00:01:10.857 --> 00:01:14.400
The row lists the dependencies, Liquid and Shortcodes.

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:16.092
Select Enable.

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:20.883
A notification confirms it, and the Design menu gets a Shortcodes entry.

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:28.663
This template is based on an example in the documentation.

00:01:28.663 --> 00:01:32.411
If the shortcode has a text argument, the template prints it.

00:01:32.411 --> 00:01:35.543
Otherwise, it prints the content between the tags.

00:01:36.293 --> 00:01:38.402
Liquid encodes every output.

00:01:38.402 --> 00:01:43.734
The template captures its markup, cleans it with the sanitize HTML filter, which

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:49.253
removes unsafe markup, and writes it with the raw filter, which skips the encoding.

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:53.145
Open Design, Shortcodes.

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:57.383
The list is empty, so select Add Shortcode Template.

00:01:59.348 --> 00:02:03.801
Name is what editors type between the brackets, so type primary.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:09.208
The name is mandatory, it must be valid inside brackets, and it must be unique.

00:02:09.673 --> 00:02:14.396
Hint describes the shortcode, and Usage shows how to write it, in HTML.

00:02:14.396 --> 00:02:18.813
A preview card follows what you type, as it appears in the picker.

00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:23.825
Categories group shortcodes in the picker, so select HTML Content.

00:02:23.825 --> 00:02:29.737
Default Shortcode Value is the text the picker inserts, here a shortcode with some text.

00:02:30.196 --> 00:02:32.433
Content takes the Liquid template.

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:37.466
Orchard Core checks it when you save, and reports an error if it isn't valid Liquid.

00:02:37.944 --> 00:02:38.906
Select Save.

00:02:38.906 --> 00:02:42.384
The list shows the template with its hint and its category.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.195
From the list, you can search templates by name, edit one, delete it,

00:02:47.195 --> 00:02:50.040
or select several and delete them together.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.436
Edit an article, and put the cursor in the body.

00:02:57.436 --> 00:03:01.890
The Insert Shortcode button of the editor opens Available Shortcodes.

00:03:02.372 --> 00:03:06.803
The list holds the shortcodes registered in code, and your templates.

00:03:06.803 --> 00:03:10.347
The primary shortcode appears with its hint and usage.

00:03:10.347 --> 00:03:11.352
Select Add.

00:03:11.943 --> 00:03:15.218
The editor inserts the default value into the body.

00:03:15.218 --> 00:03:17.343
Publish the article to save it.

00:03:18.332 --> 00:03:22.568
On the page, the shortcode is replaced by the output of the template:

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:25.392
the text, in the primary color of the theme.

00:03:29.592 --> 00:03:32.345
To read the content item, use Context.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:37.600
This template, also based on the documentation, prints the display text of the

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.852
item that holds the shortcode.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:44.732
Html and Markdown body parts and fields fill in Context dot ContentItem.

00:03:45.482 --> 00:03:50.005
A template with the same name as a shortcode from code, such as

00:03:50.005 --> 00:03:53.937
image, replaces it, because templates are asked first.

00:03:53.937 --> 00:03:59.902
And an Html Body part with Sanitize Html on cleans the HTML after the shortcodes run.

00:04:00.652 --> 00:04:04.852
In your own views, the shortcode filter in Liquid and the Orchard helper

00:04:04.852 --> 00:04:08.352
in Razor render the shortcodes of any string you give them.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.705
Templates also travel as data.

00:04:14.705 --> 00:04:20.565
The ShortcodeTemplates recipe step creates them, keyed by name, with the fields of the form.

00:04:20.565 --> 00:04:27.382
When Deployment is enabled, the All Shortcode Templates deployment step exports every template as that step.

00:04:28.132 --> 00:04:32.393
Managing templates takes the Manage shortcode templates permission.

00:04:32.393 --> 00:04:35.720
It is security critical, so assign it with caution.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.222
The Administrator and Editor roles have it by default.

00:04:41.222 --> 00:04:43.062
That's Shortcode Templates:

00:04:43.062 --> 00:04:48.582
your own shortcodes, written in Liquid, with arguments, content and the content item at hand.

00:04:48.582 --> 00:04:50.032
Thanks for watching.

